      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "classified_as": [
        {
          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "lace, a string or cord serving to draw together opposite edges of clothing (bodices, stays, boots, shoes) by being passed through eyelet-holes or over hooks and pulled tight (OED s.v. lace n. 3); here measured in gross — so not lace n. 6 (the openwork fabric, measured in yards). Made of thread, leather, hair, worsted or caddis. For gold/silver decorative braid see passemain; see also point, scholas (shoelaces), aglett."
    }
  ],
